WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.780
Before a bakery sells a single loaf,

2
00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:06.710
it already owes 100 a day
for its ovens and rent.

3
00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:10.370
Its 3rd batch of the day
adds just 30 to its costs.

4
00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:12.880
But its 5th batch adds 80.

5
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.250
Same bakery, same day.

6
00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:17.540
Why can the next batch
of bread cost a bakery

7
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.380
more to make than the batches before it?

8
00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:23.920
In this mission, you'll build
the bakery's full cost table:

9
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:27.260
fixed, variable, average and marginal.

10
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.930
Then you'll double the rent,

11
00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:32.500
raise wages, and predict
which cost curves move.

12
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.380
Your mission: find out
what drives up the cost

13
00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:36.750
of one more batch.
